## Key Concepts
- On-device machine learning and privacy-first design
- Lightweight multilingual models for resource-constrained environments
- Explainability through keyword attribution and contribution scoring
- Offline labeling pipelines and evaluation methodologies

## Code Example
```javascript
function predict(text) {
  const keywords = extractKeywords(text);
  const embeddings = model.embed(keywords);
  const intent = classifier.predict(embeddings);
  const tone = sentimentAnalyzer.predict(embeddings);
  const explanations = explainer.attribute(keywords, intent);
  return { intent, tone, explanations };
}
```

This design meets all constraints: under 15 MB, on-device execution, multilingual support (EN/ES/PT), explainable predictions, and strong privacy controls.

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates your ability to enable rapid domain adaptation with privacy guarantees in a real-time environment, emphasizing latency constraints, privacy preservation, and robust rollback mechanisms.

## Key Concepts

- Parameter-efficient adapters (LoRA/Adapters) for domain adaptation
- On-device fine-tuning with privacy guarantees (DP or federated learning)
- Streaming drift detection and safe rollback strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: load base model, attach adapter for domain, fine-tune on small labeled set
function adaptDomain(model, domain, labeledData) {
  const adapter = new LoRAAdapter(model, { rank: 4, alpha: 8 });
  adapter.fineTune(labeledData, { privacy: 'DP-SGD', epochs: 3 });
  return adapter;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses end-to-end design from data gathering to deployment with multilingual and explainability constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Multilingual encoders with adapters
- Weak supervision labeling
- Edge deployment latency
- Explainability techniques
- Drift monitoring per language

